[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Members Low Level Requirements
UID: GSSC-MEMBERS-LOW-LEVEL-REQUIREMENTS
VERSION: 5.0.0

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: TEXT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
- TAG: SECTION
  PROPERTIES:
    IS_COMPOSITE: True
    PREFIX: None
    VIEW_STYLE: Narrative
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  PROPERTIES:
    PREFIX: GSSC-MLLR-
    VIEW_STYLE: Table
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: RATIONALE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: COMMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: DERIVED
    TYPE: SingleChoice(True, False)
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: VERIFICATION_METHOD
    TYPE: SingleChoice(Test, Inspection)
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: CHANGE_DRIVER
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: REVIEW_STATUS
    TYPE: SingleChoice(Changed, Approved, Baselined)
    REQUIRED: True
  RELATIONS:
  - TYPE: Parent
    ROLE: Refines
    REVERSE_ROLE: Refined By

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-INTRODUCTION
TITLE: Introduction

[TEXT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-INTRO-FRAMEWORK
STATEMENT: >>>
GSSC5-80 scaffolds this Members LLR document and the members Vitest harness. It claims no GSSC-MLLR-* requirement UIDs (mirrors public GSSC5-39: no testing-framework LLRs).
<<<

[TEXT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-INTRO-UID-BLOCKS
STATEMENT: >>>
UID allocation for this document (coordinate parallel tickets before minting):
GSSC5-79 Member FE Root + Router owns GSSC-MLLR-1 through GSSC-MLLR-13.
GSSC5-81 Member Header owns GSSC-MLLR-14 through GSSC-MLLR-31.
GSSC5-82 Member Footer owns GSSC-MLLR-40 through GSSC-MLLR-66 (Footer chrome, contact details, Key-Value Store, and Society Contact).
GSSC5-87 Logout / Session Service owns GSSC-MLLR-67 through GSSC-MLLR-71.
GSSC5-86 Login Page owns GSSC-MLLR-72 through GSSC-MLLR-91.
GSSC5-88 Route Guards & Redirects owns GSSC-MLLR-92 through GSSC-MLLR-95.
GSSC-MLLR-32 through GSSC-MLLR-39 remain free for Wave 3 (or later) claimants.
Do not reuse numbers already claimed by another ticket.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-APP-ROOT
TITLE: Member App Root

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-APP-ROOT-ELEMENT
TITLE: App Root

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-1
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend App Root SHALL contain a Header host, a Page Outlet, and a Footer host.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The App Root composes those subelements so Header, the active Member Frontend view, and Footer share one shell. Header and Footer contents are separate requirements.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-13
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-2
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend App Root SHALL fill the entire viewport.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The App Root is the outermost shell of the Member Frontend page. Filling the viewport gives Header, page content, and Footer a full-page layout that resizes with the viewport.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-13
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-3
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend App Root SHALL use the white theme token for its background and the sans-serif theme font for its text.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The outermost Member Frontend layer uses a white background and a sans-serif default. Theme tokens supply those values.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-13
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-HEADER-HOST
TITLE: Header Host

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-4
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header host SHALL hold the Member Frontend Header.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The App Root supplies a host so Header implementation mounts in the Member Frontend shell. Header contents are separate requirements.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-13
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-15
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-5
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header host SHALL stick to the top of the viewport while the member scrolls.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Authenticated Member Frontend views keep the Header at the top. Sticking the host keeps that top placement as the member scrolls.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-15
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-6
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header host SHALL inherit the App Root font and text color theme tokens.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Header host is an empty mount for Header contents. It inherits App Root type tokens so the shell stays consistent until Header paints its own presentation. Independent Header host colors are not set yet.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-15
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-FOOTER-HOST
TITLE: Footer Host

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-7
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Footer host SHALL hold the Member Frontend Footer.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The App Root supplies a host so Footer implementation mounts in the Member Frontend shell. Footer contents are separate requirements.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-13
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-20
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-8
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Footer host SHALL sit at the bottom of the App Root.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Authenticated Member Frontend views place the Footer at the bottom. The host anchors that placement in the App Root.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-20
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-9
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Footer host SHALL inherit the App Root font and text color theme tokens.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Footer host is an empty mount for Footer contents. It inherits App Root type tokens so the shell stays consistent until Footer paints its own presentation. Independent Footer host colors are not set yet.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-20
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-PAGE-OUTLET
TITLE: Page Outlet

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-10
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Page Outlet SHALL render the active Member Frontend page.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Member Frontend pages mount through the Page Outlet so each page shares the App Root shell. Page contents are separate requirements.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-13
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-11
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Page Outlet SHALL sit between the Header host and the Footer host and SHALL grow to fill the remaining App Root space.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Placing the outlet between the hosts and letting it grow keeps Header and Footer at the edges while page content uses the middle of the shell as the viewport resizes.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-13
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-12
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Page Outlet SHALL inherit the App Root font and text color theme tokens.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Page Outlet is a mount for page contents. It inherits App Root type tokens so pages share the shell defaults until a page sets its own presentation. Independent Page Outlet colors are not set yet.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-13
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-ROUTER
TITLE: Member Router

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-13
TITLE: Home Page Route
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Router SHALL open the Member Frontend home page at the root path.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Member Frontend home page for a logged-in member is the dashboard destination. This route places that home page at the root path so navigation and redirects share one entry.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-26
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-HEADER
TITLE: Member Header

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-HEADER-BAR
TITLE: Header

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-14
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Header SHALL present the Header Logo, and when a member is logged in SHALL present the Header Navigation, the Header Greeting, and the Header Logout control, and when no member is logged in SHALL present the Header Login control.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Header composes those displayed elements in the Header host. Each element's behavior is a separate requirement. This is Member Frontend chrome with login and logout affordances, not a Public Frontend Header action-bar clone.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-15
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-15
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Header SHALL fill the Header host and arrange identity, navigation, and account-access controls in a horizontal bar that wraps as the viewport narrows.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Header host already sticks to the top of the viewport. Filling that host and wrapping the bar keeps Header contents available as the page resizes.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-15
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-16
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Header SHALL use the light-green theme token for its background, the gray theme token for a thicker bottom border, and the dark-green theme token for its text.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Theme tokens keep Header presentation aligned with the organization palette shared with the Public Frontend Header. A fuller color role map for the Member Header is not set yet beyond these token choices.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-15
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-HEADER-LOGO
TITLE: Header Logo

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-17
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Logo SHALL display the GSSC Logo, and selection of the Header Logo SHALL open the Member Frontend dashboard.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Header always includes the GSSC Logo so the member can identify the society. Selecting the logo returns the member to the Member Frontend dashboard home.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-16
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-18
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Logo SHALL appear at the start of the Header in every layout.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Leading placement keeps the logo visible as the primary identity mark in the Member Header.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-16
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-19
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Logo SHALL use the dark-green theme token for its mark color.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A single theme token keeps the mark readable on the Header background until a brand color role is set.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-16
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-HEADER-NAV
TITLE: Header Navigation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-20
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
When a member is logged in, the Header Navigation SHALL provide a control that opens the Member Frontend dashboard and a control for each other Member Frontend area that member is permitted to open.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Logged-in members reach the dashboard and permitted Member Frontend areas from the Header. Area inventory grows as those areas land; this requirement covers the navigation affordance, not Public Frontend Contact or Site Search controls.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-19
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-21
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Navigation SHALL appear after the Header Logo when a member is logged in, and SHALL be omitted when no member is logged in.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Navigation sits with identity for logged-in members. Omitting it when logged out keeps the Header focused on login until authentication succeeds.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-19
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-22
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Navigation SHALL use the sans-serif theme font and the dark-green theme token for its text color.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Navigation shares Header text tokens until a fuller control style map exists.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-19
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-HEADER-GREETING
TITLE: Header Greeting

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-23
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
When a member is logged in with a valid Member Frontend session, the Header Greeting SHALL display a greeting that includes that member's name.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The greeting shows a logged-in member that the Header recognizes the session and identifies the member by name.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-17
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-24
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Greeting SHALL appear among the Header account-access controls when a member is logged in, and SHALL be omitted when no member is logged in.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Greeting is the logged-in account-access signal. Omitting it when logged out leaves room for the Header Login control.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-17
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-25
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Greeting SHALL use the sans-serif theme font and the dark-green theme token for its text color.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Greeting shares Header account-access text tokens so it reads with Login and Logout.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-17
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-HEADER-LOGOUT
TITLE: Header Logout

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-26
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
When a member is logged in, the Header Logout control SHALL end that member's Login Token session and leave the visitor logged out.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Logout ends the Unified Backend Login Token session for that member and clears Member Frontend logged-in presentation. Full route-guard redirects after logout are separate requirements.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-18
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-9
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-27
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Logout control SHALL appear among the Header account-access controls when a member is logged in, and SHALL be omitted when no member is logged in.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Logout sits with the Greeting for logged-in members and is hidden when there is no session to end.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-18
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-28
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Logout control SHALL use the sans-serif theme font and the dark-green theme token for its text color.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Account-access controls share Header text tokens until a fuller control style map exists.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-18
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-HEADER-LOGIN
TITLE: Header Login

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-29
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
When no member is logged in, the Header Login control SHALL navigate the visitor to the Member Frontend login experience.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Login on the Member Header is navigation to the login experience. Login page contents and route guards are separate requirements.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-60
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-30
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Login control SHALL appear among the Header account-access controls when no member is logged in, and SHALL be omitted when a member is logged in.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Login replaces Greeting and Logout when there is no session. Omitting it when logged in avoids offering login to an authenticated member.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-60
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-31
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Login control SHALL use the sans-serif theme font and the dark-green theme token for its text color.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Account-access controls share Header text tokens until a fuller control style map exists.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-60
  ROLE: Refines

