[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-AUTHENTICATION
TITLE: Authentication

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-SESSION-SERVICE
TITLE: Session Service

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-67
TITLE: Session Challenge
STATEMENT: >>>
The Member Frontend Session Service SHALL determine whether a visitor is logged in by challenging the Unified Backend Login Token session and, when the challenge reports a valid session with a member identifier, loading that member's account view for Member Frontend display.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Session state comes from the Unified Backend cookie challenge rather than a Member Frontend-stored Login Token. The account view supplies the display name used by Header Greeting and other authenticated chrome.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-87
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-7
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-68
TITLE: Invalid Session
STATEMENT: >>>
When the Login Token session challenge reports an invalid or absent session, or the account view cannot be loaded, the Member Frontend Session Service SHALL treat the visitor as logged out.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
An invalid or missing session must not grant Member Frontend contents. Clearing local logged-in state keeps Header and guards aligned with the Unified Backend.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-87
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-8
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-69
TITLE: Login Credentials Submission
STATEMENT: >>>
The Member Frontend Session Service SHALL submit a member's username or primary email together with that member's password to the Unified Backend login when the Login Page requests authentication.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Unified Backend accepts either username or primary email with a password. The Session Service is the Member Frontend owner of that credentialed login call.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-87
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-4
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-70
TITLE: Login Success Session
STATEMENT: >>>
When Unified Backend login succeeds, the Member Frontend Session Service SHALL treat the member as logged in after challenging the Login Token session and loading the member account view.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A successful login has to establish usable Member Frontend session state without minting a Login Token in the Member Frontend. Challenge plus account view hydrate display state after the cookie is set.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-87
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-5
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-71
TITLE: Login Failure Session
STATEMENT: >>>
When Unified Backend login fails, the Member Frontend Session Service SHALL leave the visitor logged out.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A failed login must not grant Member Frontend contents. The Login Page shows failure feedback; this requirement covers session state only.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-87
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-6
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

